Q: Mapster mapping issue. Mapping a list of objects to a list of strings A: <p>As Mapster says, when mapping to strings it will use ToString or Parse to perform the mapping:</p>

<pre><code>var s = 123.Adapt&lt;string&gt;(); //equal to 123.ToString(); 
var i = "123".Adapt&lt;int&gt;();  //equal to int.Parse("123");
</code></pre>

<p>so you will need to implement a conversion routine that tells mapster how to parse from String to RolesViewModel.</p>

Q: Exception in thread &quot;main&quot; java.lang.NoClassDefFoundError: org/jvnet/staxex/XMLStreamReaderEx A: <p>I also had a same issue, Above post helped me at least go near the error and understand it.</p>

<p>And after some analysis. I just upgraded the Jaws-rt  Jar version it resolved my issue.</p>

<p>By the time I using Jaws-rt jar below maven dependency i used.</p>

<pre><code>   &lt;dependency&gt;
        &lt;groupId&gt;com.sun.xml.ws&lt;/groupId&gt;
        &lt;artifactId&gt;jaxws-rt&lt;/artifactId&gt;
        &lt;version&gt;2.3.2&lt;/version&gt;
    &lt;/dependency&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: Configuration failures resulting into Test skip in TestNG with no information in XMLs A: <p>Did you assign test listeners to your test?</p>

<pre><code>    &lt;?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?&gt;
&lt;!DOCTYPE suite SYSTEM "http://testng.org/testng-1.0.dtd"&gt;
&lt;suite name="Group D - Using variables" parallel="false" preserve-order="true"&gt;
  &lt;listeners&gt;    
    &lt;listener class-name="com.reportng.JUnitXMLReporter"/&gt;
  &lt;/listeners&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>The test listener is catching all the failures and skipped steps / tests.</p>
